            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A rectangle has one side of length 20 cm and its diagonal has length 25 cm. Find the length of the other side.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$15\\text{ cm}$",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the length of the other side, measured in centimetres. The diagonal is the hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+20^2&=25^2\\\\x^2+400&=625\\\\x^2&=625-400\\\\x^2&=225\\\\x&=15\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe other side is $15\\text{ cm}$ long.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
